---
// TvGuideView — the dedicated FULLSCREEN programme Guide (W4, 0.9.0).
//
// Four modes, one screen (default On Now — the timeline grid is
// demoted to the secondary "Full Guide" tab, never the default):
//
//   On Now     — mockup 3's composition: featured programme on
//                the left (art + title + times + synopsis, following
//                the focused row) and a compact channel Now/Next
//                list on the right. Polished TV listings, not a
//                data table and never stacked full-width rows.
//   Tonight    — RTÉ Guide-style evening (17:00–23:00 local):
//                art-led featured programme + gated sections, all
//                from real EPG metadata (see livetv-tonight.ts).
//                Featured art comes only from W2's enrichment API
//                (enrichProgramme, featured programmes only) —
//                never invented; without it the featured slot is a
//                channel-branded gradient, never a giant initial.
//   By Channel — one channel's schedule as a simple chronological
//                sequence; LB/RB moves days (-7..+14).
//   Full Guide — the 0.8.0 timeline grid, unchanged engine, kept
//                only as the secondary tab. 0.11.0 W6 fixed its
//                rendering: the grid's rows/cells/ticks are injected
//                by the client script, so their rules are :global
//                in the <style> below — scoped selectors never
//                matched them and the tab rendered empty.
//
// Mounts into `#livetv-mode-guide` on livetv.astro (this component's
// root carries `data-livetv-guide-root`, NOT the mount id, so there
// is exactly one `#livetv-mode-guide` in the DOM).
//
// Data: cached channels (`readCachedLiveChannels`) + cached EPG
// (`getProgrammesSync`) — the EPG engine is reused, never rewritten.
// All Guide logic is pure and testable over programme arrays
// (livetv-guide.ts / livetv-tonight.ts); the component only hands
// real data in. The short-EPG cache is in-memory and not seedable,
// so headless renders show the honest empty state, never fake rows.
//
// Rows are built inline by `programmeRowHtml` ({ programme,
// channel, variant: "now" | "tonight" | "channel" }, plus the next
// programme for On Now). INTEGRATION NOTE: the shared
// TvProgrammeRow Astro component cannot be swapped in here —
// Guide rows are client-side HTML strings (innerHTML), and an
// Astro component cannot render inside a <script> string builder.
// The inline builder instead carries the same visual contract
// (logo tile + title + time + progress + next line, same hooks
// shape) and the Guide-specific data the shared row does not
// model (programme desc, honestly-gated catch-up badge, LIVE
// state, data-focus-key). Catch-up stays gated by
// guideCellViewModel, never invented.
//
// Actions dispatch the shared Live TV events — the Guide never
// plays anything itself:
//   livetv:tune {channelId} + requestLivetvMode("playback") — watch live
//   livetv:programme {channelId, startMs} — catch-up replay / restart.
//     startMs is the DISPLAY time, matching TvQuickSurf's dispatch;
//     whoever plays it converts with displayedToUtcMs, as epg.ts does.
//   requestLivetvMode(returnTo) — leaving the Guide
//   (returnTo = the mode the Guide was entered from, recorded in
//   shared state as guideReturnTo; "landing" default)
// Mode switching: `livetv:mode` {mode:"guide", guideMode} —
// guideMode lives in the SHARED state (livetv-state.ts); this
// component keeps a local working copy that is seeded from
// liveState on entry and written back on every tab change.
// B: the Guide listens for the `livetv:back` window event (W5's
// contract) and the guide "back" key action — detail open closes
// first, otherwise the Guide exits to its entry mode.
// While active the Guide sets html[data-livetv-mode="guide"] (the
// same marker pattern TvPlaybackShell uses for "playback") so
// gamepad.ts routes X / Y / LB / RB / Menu to the Guide.
// Catch-up is offered ONLY where `catchupActionForProgramme` says so.
//
// 0.11.7 (W3) — Guide virtualisation + shared category model.
// AUDIT (§1D), per mode, as found on the 0.11.5 base:
//   On Now     — renderNow() built EVERY Now/Next row with one
//                innerHTML (up to one button per channel). FIXED:
//                spacer-virtualised, keyed rows, rAF on scroll.
//   Tonight    — editorial sections are capped (8/section, ≤48
//                rows) and stay fully rendered; the chronological
//                fallback rendered the WHOLE evening uncapped
//                (thousands of rows). FIXED: the fallback is a
//                focus-window virtual list in its own container.
//   By Channel — renderChannelList() built a button per visible
//                channel with one innerHTML. FIXED: spacer-
//                virtualised picker. The schedule (one channel,
//                one day) is bounded by nature and stays fully
//                rendered; it never rebuilds on scroll.
//   Full Guide — already windowed both ways (epgRowWindow +
//                epgTimeWindow) with rAF scroll rendering.
//                IMPROVED: rebuilds are skipped when the window
//                signature is unchanged, and the focused cell
//                survives rebuilds (focus preservation).
// Categories come ONLY from the shared category index, through
// the single adapter in livetv-guide-categories.ts — the old
// raw-category <select> (a second, contradictory categorisation)
// is replaced by the controller-first category drawer
// (livetv-guide-category-picker.ts, built on W2's shared drawer
// module livetv-category-drawer.ts — the same drawer the Channel
// Browser uses). A channel selected in the Guide is
// identifiable in the Browser via the `livetv:guide-channel`
// event (see selectProgramme) — highlight-only, never tunes.
import TvProgrammeMeta from "./TvProgrammeMeta.astro";

interface Props {
  /** Active playlist id; resolved via getActiveEntry() when omitted. */
  playlistId?: string;
}
const { playlistId = "" } = Astro.props;
const nowMs = Date.now();
---

<section
  class="rs-livetv-guide"
  data-livetv-guide-root
  data-playlist-id={playlistId}
  aria-label="Programme guide"
  hidden
>
  <!-- Tab row: the four Guide modes + search. Left/Right on the
       tabs switches mode; the category filter serves On Now and
       By Channel. -->
  <div class="rs-guide-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Guide views">
    <button
      type="button"
      class="rs-livetv-guide__toolbtn"
      data-guide-back
      aria-label="Back from guide"
    >
      ← Back
    </button>
    <button
      type="button"
      role="tab"
      class="rs-guide-tab rs-guide-tab--active"
      data-guide-tab="now"
      aria-selected="true"
    >
      On Now
    </button>
    <button
      type="button"
      role="tab"
      class="rs-guide-tab"
      data-guide-tab="tonight"
      aria-selected="false"
      tabindex="-1"
    >
      Tonight
    </button>
    <button
      type="button"
      role="tab"
      class="rs-guide-tab"
      data-guide-tab="channel"
      aria-selected="false"
      tabindex="-1"
    >
      By Channel
    </button>
    <button
      type="button"
      role="tab"
      class="rs-guide-tab"
      data-guide-tab="grid"
      aria-selected="false"
      tabindex="-1"
    >
      Full Guide
    </button>
    <label class="rs-guide-searchlabel">
      <span class="rs-guide-searchlabel-text">Search</span>
      <input
        type="search"
        class="rs-guide-search"
        data-guide-search
        placeholder="Search programmes…"
        aria-label="Search programmes"
      />
    </label>
    <button
      type="button"
      class="rs-livetv-guide__toolbtn rs-guide-category-trigger"
      data-guide-category-trigger
      aria-haspopup="dialog"
      aria-expanded="false"
      aria-label="Choose channel category"
    >
      Category: <span data-guide-category-trigger-label>All categories</span>
    </button>
  </div>

  <!-- Category drawer mount (0.11.7): the drawer panel is rendered
       here by livetv-guide-category-picker.ts (W2's shared drawer
       module) — the mount is display:contents
       so the panel positions against the Guide root. -->
  <div data-guide-category-drawer></div>

  <!-- MODE A — On Now (default): mockup 3's Guide composition —
       featured programme on the left (photo + title + times +
       synopsis), channel Now/Next list on the right. Never a
       stacked full-width list. -->
  <div
    class="rs-guide-panel rs-guide-panel--now"
    data-guide-panel="now"
    role="tabpanel"
    aria-label="On now"
  >
    <div class="rs-guide-now">
      <div class="rs-guide-now-featured" data-guide-now-featured hidden></div>
      <div class="rs-guide-now-listwrap">
        <div class="rs-guide-now-head" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="rs-guide-now-head__channel">Channel</span>
          <span class="rs-guide-now-head__now">Now</span>
          <span class="rs-guide-now-head__next">Next</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rs-guide-list rs-guide-now-list" data-guide-now-list></div>
        <p class="rs-guide-panel-empty" data-guide-now-empty hidden>
          Nothing on now — the guide hasn't loaded yet. Open Live TV first
          so the channel list and programme data load.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- MODE B — Tonight: featured programme + gated sections. -->
  <div
    class="rs-guide-panel"
    data-guide-panel="tonight"
    role="tabpanel"
    aria-label="Tonight"
    hidden
  >
    <div class="rs-guide-tonight-featured" data-guide-tonight-featured hidden></div>
    <div class="rs-guide-tonight-sections" data-guide-tonight-sections></div>
    <!-- Chronological fallback (0.11.7): the uncapped evening list
         renders here as a focus-window virtual list — never in the
         sections container, which keeps the capped sections. -->
    <div class="rs-guide-tonight-fallback" data-guide-tonight-fallback hidden></div>
    <p class="rs-guide-panel-empty" data-guide-tonight-empty hidden>
      No evening listings yet — the guide hasn't loaded, or tonight's
      programmes have finished.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- MODE C — By Channel: channel picker + chronological schedule. -->
  <div
    class="rs-guide-panel rs-guide-panel--channel"
    data-guide-panel="channel"
    role="tabpanel"
    aria-label="By channel"
    hidden
  >
    <div class="rs-guide-channel-picker" data-guide-channel-picker>
      <div class="rs-guide-channel-list" data-guide-channel-list></div>
    </div>
    <div class="rs-guide-channel-schedule">
      <div class="rs-guide-channel-daynav">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="rs-livetv-guide__toolbtn rs-livetv-guide__toolbtn--square"
          data-guide-channel-prev-day
          aria-label="Previous day"
        >
          ‹
        </button>
        <span
          class="rs-livetv-guide__daylabel"
          data-guide-channel-day-label
          aria-live="polite"
        >
          Today
        </span>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="rs-livetv-guide__toolbtn rs-livetv-guide__toolbtn--square"
          data-guide-channel-next-day
          aria-label="Next day"
        >
          ›
        </button>
        <span class="rs-guide-channel-dayhint" data-guide-channel-dayhint>
          LB / RB changes day
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="rs-guide-list" data-guide-channel-schedule></div>
      <p class="rs-guide-panel-empty" data-guide-channel-empty hidden>
        No programmes listed for this channel on this day.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- MODE D — Full Guide (secondary): the 0.8.0 timeline grid,
       engine unchanged. Grid-only toolbar: day nav + Jump to Now. -->
  <div
    class="rs-guide-panel"
    data-guide-panel="grid"
    role="tabpanel"
    aria-label="Full guide"
    hidden
  >
    <div class="rs-livetv-guide__toolbar" role="toolbar" aria-label="Guide controls">
      <button
        type="button"
        class="rs-livetv-guide__toolbtn rs-livetv-guide__toolbtn--square"
        data-guide-prev-day
        aria-label="Previous day"
      >
        ‹
      </button>
      <span
        class="rs-livetv-guide__daylabel"
        data-guide-day-label
        aria-live="polite"
      >
        Today
      </span>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="rs-livetv-guide__toolbtn rs-livetv-guide__toolbtn--square"
        data-guide-next-day
        aria-label="Next day"
      >
        ›
      </button>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="rs-livetv-guide__toolbtn"
        data-guide-now
      >
        Now
      </button>
      <span class="rs-livetv-guide__hint" data-guide-hint>
        LB / RB shifts time · N jumps to now
      </span>
    </div>

    <div
      class="rs-livetv-guide__scroll"
      data-guide-scroll
      tabindex="-1"
    >
      <div class="rs-livetv-guide__track" data-guide-track>
        <div class="rs-livetv-guide__head">
          <div class="rs-livetv-guide__corner" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div
            class="rs-livetv-guide__timehead"
            data-guide-timehead
            aria-hidden="true"
          ></div>
        </div>
        <div class="rs-livetv-guide__body" data-guide-body></div>
        <div
          class="rs-livetv-guide__nowline"
          data-guide-nowline
          aria-hidden="true"
          hidden
        ></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Contextual detail for the selected programme. The meta block
       starts hidden (no fake times) and is filled by the script. -->
  <div class="rs-livetv-guide__detail" data-guide-detail>
    <p class="rs-livetv-guide__detail-empty" data-guide-detail-empty>
      Select a programme to see details.
    </p>
    <div
      class="rs-livetv-guide__detail-meta"
      data-guide-detail-meta
      hidden
    >
      <TvProgrammeMeta
        title="Select a programme"
        startMs={nowMs}
        stopMs={nowMs + 3600000}
        desc="Choose a programme to see details."
        catchup
      />
    </div>
    <div class="rs-livetv-guide__actions" data-guide-actions>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="rs-livetv-guide__action"
        data-guide-action-watch
        hidden
      >
        Watch live
      </button>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="rs-livetv-guide__action rs-livetv-guide__action--catchup"
        data-guide-action-catchup
        hidden
      >
        Replay
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div
    class="rs-livetv-guide__empty"
    data-guide-empty
    role="status"
    hidden
  >
    <p data-guide-empty-text>Loading the programme guide…</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .rs-livetv-guide {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 0;
    color: var(--rs-text);
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__toolbar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__toolbtn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 3rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.9rem;
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rs-line);
    background: var(--rs-bg-2);
    color: var(--rs-text);
    font-family: var(--rs-font-body);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__toolbtn:hover {
    background: var(--rs-surface-2);
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__toolbtn--square {
    padding-inline: 0.7rem;
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__toolbtn:disabled {
    opacity: 0.4;
    cursor: default;
  }
  .rs-guide-category-trigger [data-guide-category-trigger-label] {
    font-weight: 600;
    max-width: 16rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__daylabel {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--rs-text-2);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    white-space: nowrap;
    padding-inline: 0.25rem;
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__hint {
    margin-left: auto;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--rs-text-2);
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__scroll {
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 0;
    overflow: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--rs-line);
    border-radius: 1.25rem;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--rs-surface) 0%, var(--rs-bg) 18rem);
    box-shadow: var(--rs-shadow);
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__track {
    position: relative;
    min-width: max-content;
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__head {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 30;
    display: flex;
    align-items: stretch;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rs-line);
    background: var(--rs-surface);
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__corner {
    position: sticky;
    left: 0;
    z-index: 31;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 240px;
    height: 40px;
    background: var(--rs-surface);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--rs-line);
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__timehead {
    position: relative;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    height: 40px;
  }
  /* Grid rules below are :global — the grid's rows, cells and
     ticks are injected by the client script (innerHTML), so they
     never carry Astro's scope attribute and scoped selectors
     would never match them (0.11.0 W6: the Full Guide tab rendered
     completely empty — cells in the DOM, no styles applied —
     because of exactly that; the 0.9.0/0.10.0 passes never
     screenshotted the grid, so it went unnoticed). Static grid
     chrome (toolbar, scroll, track, head, body, nowline) stays
     scoped. */
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__tick) {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    padding: 0.5rem 0 0 0.5rem;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--rs-line);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--rs-text-2);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__body {
    position: relative;
  }
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__row) {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: stretch;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rs-line);
    content-visibility: auto;
    contain-intrinsic-size: auto 4.75rem;
  }
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__channel) {
    position: sticky;
    left: 0;
    z-index: 10;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 240px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    background: var(--rs-bg-2);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--rs-line);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__channel--focused) {
    background: linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--rs-accent) 14%, transparent),
      var(--rs-bg-2)
    );
    box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 var(--rs-accent);
  }
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__logo) {
    width: 3rem;
    height: 3rem;
    object-fit: contain;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    background: var(--rs-surface-2);
  }
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__logo--fallback) {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--rs-text);
  }
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__channel-name) {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--rs-text);
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__catchup-dot) {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.55rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--rs-accent) 25%, transparent);
    color: var(--rs-focus);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--rs-accent) 50%, transparent);
  }
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__cells) {
    position: relative;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__cell) {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.375rem;
    bottom: 0.375rem;
    min-width: 2px;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rs-line);
    border-radius: 0.6rem;
    background: var(--rs-surface);
    color: var(--rs-text);
    font-family: var(--rs-font-body);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
    text-align: left;
    overflow: hidden;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__cell-title) {
    display: block;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__cell-time) {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--rs-text-2);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__cell--now) {
    background: linear-gradient(
      135deg,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--rs-accent) 26%, transparent),
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--rs-focus) 12%, transparent)
    );
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--rs-accent) 45%, transparent),
      0 0 1.125rem 0.125rem color-mix(in srgb, var(--rs-accent) 22%, transparent);
  }
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__cell--past) {
    opacity: 0.62;
  }
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__cell--catchup)::after {
    content: "↺";
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.2rem;
    right: 0.45rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--rs-focus);
  }
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__cell):focus-visible {
    z-index: 5;
    outline: none;
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 2px var(--rs-focus),
      0 0 2rem 0.25rem var(--rs-focus-glow);
  }
  :global(.rs-livetv-guide__cell--selected) {
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--rs-focus);
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__nowline {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 2px;
    z-index: 20;
    background: var(--rs-accent);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0.75rem 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--rs-accent) 60%, transparent);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__detail {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rs-line);
    border-radius: 1.25rem;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--rs-surface), var(--rs-bg-2));
    box-shadow: var(--rs-shadow);
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
    min-height: 5.5rem;
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__detail-empty {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--rs-text-2);
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__detail-meta {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .rs-livetv-guide__action {
    min-height: 3.25rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rs-line);
    background: var(--rs-accent);
    color: var(--rs-text);
    font-family: var(--rs-font-body);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
